Feature: Decoding Zstandard frames
  The frames of the fixed scenarios are written from RFC 8878 or made by the reference `zstd` command line. The frames
  of the peer scenarios come from `fixtures/zstd_peer.py`, which drives that command line: every level and window it
  has, with and without a checksum or a content size, several frames in a row, and damaged frames on which the codec
  and `zstd -d` must give the same answer.

